- op: discuss  # 0d99
  at: '2026-08-05T06:22:35Z'  # 0d99
  by: agent  # 0d99
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0d99
  clock: 4  # 0d99
  nonce: 0d99  # 0d99
  message: "GROUP 1 PARTLY SHIPPED in PR #213, and the package surfaces were READ rather than assumed - which changed two of the three answers. ujson: exposes dump/dumps/load/loads, so it mirrors the catalogued json.dump file-write. CATALOGUED. orjson: exposes only dumps/loads, NO dump, so it has no file-write surface at all and cataloguing it would match nothing - EXCLUDED, and pinned by a test so a later completeness pass does not add it by symmetry with ujson. defusedcsv: BLOCKED, and not by the catalogue. Its real API is the defusedcsv.csv SUBMODULE (top level exposes only `version`), but the analyzer emits module=defusedcsv name=csv.writer for the pretix shape. Tested both declarations against the live edge through production _match_propagation_entry: the conventional form (module defusedcsv.csv, functions [writer]) does NOT match; only a dotted NAME does, a form used by exactly 1 of 1979 built-in primitives. Filed as an analyzer module/name split defect rather than encoding the defect into the catalogue. Remaining here: defusedcsv once that lands, plus the group-2 items (django.core.files.storage default_storage.*, tarfile, zipfile) which are genuine uncatalogued primitives rather than wrappers and deserve their own item."  # 0d99
